# Build output
bin/
dist/

# Runtime state a contributor may create by running Otter in this checkout: the
# SQLite database, extracted SDK, releases, serve records and lock. Using Otter
# for real means running it in your own directory, not this one, so none of it
# is ever committed.
.otter/
tmp/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Job identity markers. The runtime writes one into a job
# directory; it names a local instance, so a fresh clone registering its own is
# the intended behaviour and the file stays out of git.
.otter-id
.otter-id.tmp-*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Tool caches
.cache/
.gocache/

# Task worktrees. Phase 0 runs one isolated worker per task, each in its own
# worktree and branch under this directory; the branches are what get merged, so
# the working copies themselves are never committed. The leading dot also keeps
# them out of `go`'s ./... traversal. See docs/phase-0-execution-plan.md.
.worktrees/

# Environment files. A contributor testing a runtime here may create one; the
# values are credentials, so nothing named like an env file is committed, and a
# template is excluded too because git cannot tell a filled-in one from a
# placeholder.
otter.daemon.env
otter.env
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.*
!*.env.example

# Local logs and editor state
run.log
.nvimlog
*.log

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
